<?xml version='1.0' encoding='UTF-8'?>
<!DOCTYPE reference PUBLIC "-//OASIS//DTD DITA Reference//EN" "reference.dtd">
<reference id="callback_imediaplayersourceobserver_onplayersourcestatechanged">
    <title><ph keyref="onPlayerSourceStateChanged"/></title>
    <shortdesc id="short"><ph id="shortdesc" props="cpp">Callback for playback state changes.</ph><ph id="shortdesc" props="android">Callback for playback state changes.</ph></shortdesc>
    <prolog>
        <metadata>
            <keywords>
                <indexterm keyref="onPlayerSourceStateChanged"/>
            </keywords>
        </metadata>
    </prolog>
    <refbody>
        <section id="prototype">
            <p outputclass="codeblock">
                <codeblock props="cpp" outputclass="language-cpp">virtual void onPlayerSourceStateChanged(media::base::MEDIA_PLAYER_STATE state, media::base::MEDIA_PLAYER_REASON reason) = 0;</codeblock>
                <codeblock props="android" outputclass="language-java">void onPlayerStateChanged(Constants.MediaPlayerState state, Constants.MediaPlayerReason reason);</codeblock>
            </p>
        </section>
        <section id="detailed_desc" deliveryTarget="details" otherprops="no-title">
            <p props="cpp">This callback is triggered by the SDK to report the current playback state when the media player state changes.</p>
            <p props="android">This callback is triggered by the SDK when the media player's state changes.</p>
            <p props="android">For on-demand playback, <codeph>PLAYER_STATE_PLAYBACK_COMPLETED</codeph> (5) indicates that the current playback has completed and the player will continue repeating. <codeph>PLAYER_STATE_PLAYBACK_ALL_LOOPS_COMPLETED</codeph> (6) indicates that the final playback has completed.</p>
            <p props="android">Handle <codeph>PLAYER_STATE_PLAYBACK_ALL_LOOPS_COMPLETED</codeph> (6) when the entire playback session completes normally. This state is also reported after a single playback when looping is not configured. Each playback iteration reports only one completion state; the final iteration reports <codeph>PLAYER_STATE_PLAYBACK_ALL_LOOPS_COMPLETED</codeph> (6) without first reporting <codeph>PLAYER_STATE_PLAYBACK_COMPLETED</codeph> (5).</p>
        </section>
        <section id="playback_scenarios" props="android" deliveryTarget="details">
            <title>On-demand playback scenarios</title>
            <p>Only playback-completion and stop states are listed. Intermediate states such as opening and playing are omitted.</p>
            <simpletable relcolwidth="1* 1* 3*">
                <sthead><stentry>Method call</stentry><stentry>Playback behavior</stentry><stentry>State callback sequence</stentry></sthead>
                <strow><stentry>No call to <codeph>setLoopCount</codeph></stentry><stentry>Plays once</stentry><stentry>Reports <codeph>PLAYER_STATE_PLAYBACK_ALL_LOOPS_COMPLETED</codeph> (6) when playback completes.</stentry></strow>
                <strow><stentry><codeph>setLoopCount(0)</codeph></stentry><stentry>Plays once</stentry><stentry>Reports <codeph>PLAYER_STATE_PLAYBACK_ALL_LOOPS_COMPLETED</codeph> (6) when playback completes.</stentry></strow>
                <strow><stentry><codeph>setLoopCount(1)</codeph></stentry><stentry>Plays twice</stentry><stentry>Reports <codeph>PLAYER_STATE_PLAYBACK_COMPLETED</codeph> (5) after the first playback, then <codeph>PLAYER_STATE_PLAYBACK_ALL_LOOPS_COMPLETED</codeph> (6) after the second playback.</stentry></strow>
                <strow><stentry><codeph>setLoopCount(-1)</codeph></stentry><stentry>Repeats indefinitely</stentry><stentry>Reports <codeph>PLAYER_STATE_PLAYBACK_COMPLETED</codeph> (5) after each playback, then repeats.</stentry></strow>
                <strow><stentry>Successful <codeph>stop()</codeph> during playback</stentry><stentry>Stops playback</stentry><stentry>Reports <codeph>PLAYER_STATE_STOPPED</codeph> (7).</stentry></strow>
            </simpletable>
        </section>
        <section id="parameters" deliveryTarget="details" props="android cpp">
            <title>Parameters</title>
            <parml>
                <plentry props="cpp">
                    <pt>state</pt>
                    <pd>Playback state. See <xref keyref="MEDIA_PLAYER_STATE"/>.</pd>
                </plentry>
                <plentry props="cpp">
                    <pt>reason</pt>
                    <pd>Reason for the playback state change. See <xref keyref="MEDIA_PLAYER_REASON"/>.</pd>
                </plentry>
                <plentry props="android">
                    <pt>state</pt>
                    <pd>Playback state. See <xref keyref="MEDIA_PLAYER_STATE"/>.</pd>
                </plentry>
                <plentry props="android">
                    <pt>reason</pt>
                    <pd>Reason for the playback state change. See <xref keyref="MEDIA_PLAYER_REASON"/>.</pd>
                </plentry>
            </parml>
        </section>
    </refbody>
</reference>
